  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria has two labour Centres &#x2013; Nigeria Labour Congress and Trade Union Congress  and they have been canvassing a living wage commensurate with the prevailing cost of living, security crisis which is depriving individuals and households of income-generating opportunities and socio-economic progress. In addition, are concerns around violation of trade union rights, attacks and threats to Freedom of Association (FoA), and collective bargaining, brutality encountered by trade union leaders while advocating for workers&#x2019; rights. The combined effects of these challenges are growing inequality in that has emerged as a major concern to workers. 
The ILO is implementing a project working developing the capacities of these 2 centres to influence socio-economic policies to improve the welfare of workers.

The strategy of the intervention focuses on policy advice, trainings and capacity development</narrative>
  </description>
